TITLE:: TransposeCommand
SUMMARY:: Command that adds an integer to the MIDI note number of each selected note.
CATEGORIES:: Commands
RELATED:: Classes/Command, Classes/Parameter, Classes/CommandPrompt, Classes/PianoRoll, Classes/PianoRollNote

DESCRIPTION::
TELETYPE::TransposeCommand:: is a LINK::Classes/Command:: named CODE::transpose:: that adds an integer number of semitones to each selected note. LINK::Classes/PianoRoll:: supplies the notes through LINK::Classes/CommandPrompt#-ambientParameters:: as CODE::selectedNotes::.

CODE::semitones:: is an LINK::Classes/Integer::. Positive values raise the note, negative values lower it, and zero leaves it unchanged. LINK::Classes/PianoRollNote#-transpose:: updates the wrapped LINK::Classes/PlayableNote:: and, when the note view exists, moves that view by the same number of rows.

CLASSMETHODS::

METHOD:: new
Creates a new TELETYPE::TransposeCommand::. Takes no arguments; transposition is applied by LINK::#-execute::.

RETURNS::
A new TELETYPE::TransposeCommand:: instance.

INSTANCEMETHODS::

METHOD:: execute
Adds CODE::\semitones:: to every note in CODE::\selectedNotes:: that responds to CODE::transpose::.

ARGUMENT:: args
A LINK::Classes/Dictionary:: or LINK::Classes/Event:: with CODE::\selectedNotes:: (an LINK::Classes/Array:: of notes) and CODE::\semitones:: (an LINK::Classes/Integer::).

EXAMPLES::

CODE::
(
var note = PianoRollNote(0.0, 60, 100,
	viewFunc: { View() },
	selectFunc: {},
	deselectFunc: {},
	setPart1Func: {},
	setPart2Func: {},
	setPart3Func: {},
	setPart4Func: {},
	moveFunc: {}
);
note.stop(1.0);
TransposeCommand.new.execute((
	selectedNotes: [note],
	semitones: -2
));
note.noteNumber; // 58
)
::
